BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sundance-collab-merrell-storytelling-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260818
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260819
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sundance Collab x Merrell: Brand-Supported Storytelling P
 rogram 2026
DESCRIPTION:Sundance Collab and Merrell are selecting five filmmakers from 
 around the world to each make an original 60 to 90 second vertical film fo
 r social platforms\, built around Merrell's 'It Starts Outside' brand plat
 form. The brief is not a commercial: it asks for a complete\, emotionally 
 resonant human story in which the outside acts as a catalyst for change\, 
 exploring how stepping outside is an antidote to increasingly screen-locke
 d\, indoor lives. Stories should reflect transformation (a moment of reset
 \, reconnection or personal shift)\, connection (belonging\, community\, r
 enewed relationship) and human truth (an observed\, emotionally grounded m
 oment). The strongest entries show what changed in a person because they w
 ent outside\, emotionally\, physically\, mentally\, creatively\, spiritual
 ly or psychologically\, rather than a final achievement. Selected filmmake
 rs enter a three-day online intensive in September on collaborating with a
  brand\, then receive USD 20\,000 to produce and deliver their greenlit co
 ncept\, cutdowns (:06\, :15\, :30) and stills between October and December
 \, with scheduled check-ins. One participant also receives a covered hotel
  stay to join the team at the Sundance Film Festival in January 2027. APPL
 ICATION: one entry per person\; all submitted materials must be created by
  the submitter\; all answers and materials must be in English or carry Eng
 lish subtitles. The core submission is a written response of up to 500 wor
 ds on how you would approach the brief. CRITICAL GUIDELINES: design for ve
 rtical with a strong hook in the first five seconds\; prioritise human\, o
 bservational storytelling over polished commercial aesthetics\; feature re
 al people and authentic moments\; treat the outside as context rather than
  the hero\; favour everyday\, intimate moments over epic outcomes\; avoid 
 overt brand narration\; no competitor products (Merrell product is provide
 d but must not be the focus)\; no AI-generated content in consumer-facing 
 materials. Selection criteria are originality\, emotional arc\, a distinct
  point of view and cultural relevance. TIMELINE: submissions opened 28 Jul
 y 2026\; deadline 11:59 p.m. PT on Tuesday 18 August 2026 (08:59 CEST on 1
 9 August)\; selected artists notified by 16 September 2026. An Insider Ses
 sion with Merrell Creative Director Alex Ho and Sundance Collab Director P
 atty West runs on 11 August. Sundance Collab provides accommodations and s
 upport services for participants with disabilities\; email accessibility@s
 undance.org to arrange services.\n\nOrganisation: Sundance Collab (Sundanc
 e Institute) in collaboration with Merrell\nLocation: Online program\, ope
 n to filmmakers worldwide. Production takes place wherever the filmmaker i
 s based. One participant receives a covered hotel stay at the Sundance Fil
 m Festival in Park City\, Utah\, USA in January 2027.\nAward: USD 20\,000 
 production budget per selected filmmaker to make and deliver the greenlit 
 concept\, cutdowns (:06\, :15\, :30) and stills. Includes an online brand-
 supported storytelling program\, and a covered hotel stay for one particip
 ant to attend the Sundance Film Festival in January 2027. No application f
 ee.\nDuration: Program runs September to December 2026\, with an online in
 tensive 30 September to 2 October 2026\, production in October\, post-prod
 uction in November and delivery by 14 December 2026.\n\nMore: https://coll
 ab.sundance.org/catalog/Merrell-Brand-Supported-Storytelling-Program?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://collab.sundance.org/catalog/Merrell-Brand-Supported-Storytellin
 g-Program?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online program\, open to filmmakers worldwide. Production takes pl
 ace wherever the filmmaker is based. One participant receives a covered ho
 tel stay at the Sundance Film Festival in Park City\, Utah\, USA in Januar
 y 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:knowcase-sonar-cotec-open-call-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: KNOWCASE Open Call 2027: permanent digital-culture instal
 lation in Madrid (Sonar+D x Fundacion Cotec)
DESCRIPTION:Fundacion Cotec (a Spanish innovation-focused non-profit) and S
 onar+D\, building on an initial experiment at Sonar 2026\, invite proposal
 s for a long-term installation at KNOWCASE\, the street-level showcase of 
 Cotec's Madrid headquarters in Chamberi\, visible to the public 24 hours a
  day. THEME: digital culture\, meaning projects that combine knowledge\, r
 esearch\, science and data with art\, technology and social impact. Cotec'
 s stated priorities are the big transitions (analogue to digital\, linear 
 to circular economy\, tangible to intangible) plus innovation ecosystems a
 nd R&D&I\, the climate crisis\, the future of work and learning\, social d
 ivides\, citizen participation and democratic health. WHAT YOU GET: a budg
 et of up to EUR 100\,000 plus VAT covering everything (design\, production
 \, installation\, maintenance\, documentation\, artist fees\, travel\, acc
 ommodation and insurance)\, and a minimum 24-month public display from Feb
 ruary 2027. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, collectives\, designers\, technologis
 ts\, universities\, research centres\, startups\, businesses\, creative ag
 encies\, producers\, cultural institutions and multidisciplinary teams\, i
 nternationally\; applicants must demonstrate solid experience and a releva
 nt portfolio. CONSTRAINTS: the proposal must be original and never previou
 sly exhibited\, must include participative or interactive elements\, must 
 encourage critical thinking\, and must be technically and financially viab
 le for the full 24+ month exhibition period (durability and maintenance ar
 e central selection criteria). Selection weighs conceptual quality highest
  (40 percent)\, followed by public interactivity (25 percent). HOW TO APPL
 Y: one PDF of maximum 15 pages containing summary\, concept\, technical pr
 oposal\, visuals\, budget\, timeline\, team profile\, portfolio and declar
 ation\, in Spanish\, another official language of Spain\, or English\, via
  the application portal linked from the terms and conditions. Results anno
 unced 14 October 2026. Deadline 7 September 2026 at midnight CEST.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Fundacion Cotec and Sonar+D\nLocation: Installation at the KNOWC
 ASE storefront of Fundacion Cotec's headquarters in Chamberi\, Madrid\, Sp
 ain\, a street-level venue visible 24/7. The call is international\; appli
 cations accepted in Spanish\, other official languages of Spain\, or Engli
 sh.\nAward: Up to EUR 100\,000 (plus VAT)\, all-inclusive: conceptualisati
 on\, design\, technical development\, production\, installation\, maintena
 nce\, documentation\, artist fees\, travel\, accommodation and insurance.\
 nDuration: Installation displayed for a minimum of 24 months\, starting Fe
 bruary 2027\n\nMore: https://sonar.es/en/news/knowcase-open-call-2027?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sonar.es/en/news/knowcase-open-call-2027?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Installation at the KNOWCASE storefront of Fundacion Cotec's headq
 uarters in Chamberi\, Madrid\, Spain\, a street-level venue visible 24/7. 
 The call is international\; applications accepted in Spanish\, other offic
 ial languages of Spain\, or English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kulturstiftung-des-bundes-general-project-funding-2026@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kulturstiftung des Bundes: General Project Funding (Allge
 meine Projektfoerderung)
DESCRIPTION:Germany's flagship open\, non-thematic federal project line\, a
 nd one of the largest European funders that will back a festival\, exhibit
 ion programme or multi-partner convening run by an organisation rather tha
 n an individual artist. It funds large innovative projects across all arti
 stic fields\, explicitly including New Media alongside visual and performi
 ng arts\, music\, film\, photography and architecture. There is no publish
 ed maximum\, but the EUR 50\,000 minimum total project cost sets the scale
 \, and at least 20 percent co-financing is mandatory. Deadlines are twice 
 yearly at 12:00 CET: 31 July 2026 and 31 January 2027. TIMING RULE: decisi
 ons are made by an external jury meeting in May and November\, and no proj
 ect may start before its jury date\, so plan four to six months of lead ti
 me. Non-German organisations are genuinely eligible\, which is unusual at 
 this scale\, provided the project is visible in Germany and has an interna
 tional dimension. Two practical barriers: the application form must be com
 pleted in German\, and project communications must include a German-langua
 ge version.\n\nOrganisation: Kulturstiftung des Bundes (German Federal Cul
 tural Foundation)\nLocation: Activity must be visible to audiences in Germ
 any. Institutions headquartered in Germany or abroad may apply.\nAward: No
  fixed ceiling\, but total project costs must exceed EUR 50\,000 to be eli
 gible. The Foundation allocates up to EUR 10 million per year across this 
 line. At least 20 percent of total project costs must be secured from own 
 capital and/or third-party funding. No application fee.\nDuration: Project
 -length. Projects may not begin before the jury meeting.\n\nMore: https://
 www.kulturstiftung-des-bundes.de/en/themes_focuses/general_project_funding
 .html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kulturstiftung-des-bundes.de/en/themes_focuses/general_proj
 ect_funding.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity must be visible to audiences in Germany. Institutions hea
 dquartered in Germany or abroad may apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:terra-foundation-collections-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:Deadline: Terra Foundation for American Art: Collections Grants (20
 26 cycle)
DESCRIPTION:Funds organisations to reinstall permanent collections or mount
  temporary exhibitions drawn primarily from their own holdings\, on condit
 ion the project broadens understandings of American art and pursues inclus
 ive\, expansive curatorial practice. Planning grants of USD 25\,000 to 75\
 ,000 cover research\, advisory committees and conservation\; implementatio
 n grants up to USD 100\,000 cover interpretation\, exhibition design\, con
 servation\, public programmes and dissemination of research\, so the publi
 c-programming layer of an exhibition is fundable here. TIMING: the 2026 cy
 cle is two-stage\, with a grant inquiry due 3 August 2026\, a full proposa
 l for shortlisted applicants due 13 October 2026\, external panel review\,
  decisions in April 2027 and projects starting after 1 May 2027. That is a
  nine-month decision lag\, so this is planning-horizon money. Internationa
 l applicants are explicitly welcomed and need US 501(c)(3) status or the i
 nternational equivalent. The Foundation will not fund acquisitions\, equip
 ment\, exclusively online projects\, or projects consisting primarily of l
 oans. The American-art subject requirement is the main constraint for medi
 a-arts organisations.\n\nOrganisation: Terra Foundation for American Art\n
 Location: Worldwide. Museums\, art centres and community-based cultural or
 ganisations both inside and outside the US.\nAward: Planning grants USD 25
 \,000 to 75\,000 (conservation capped at 25 percent of a planning award)\;
  implementation grants up to USD 100\,000. No formal match\, but the Found
 ation prefers not to be sole funder. No application fee.\nDuration: Projec
 t-based\; funded projects start after 1 May 2027 following April 2027 deci
 sions.\n\nMore: https://www.terraamericanart.org/what-we-offer/grant-progr
 am/collections-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.terraamericanart.org/what-we-offer/grant-program/collection
 s-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide. Museums\, art centres and community-based cultural orga
 nisations both inside and outside the US.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondazione-prada-film-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fondazione Prada Film Fund 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Fondazione Prada Film Fund is an annual initiative supporti
 ng independent cinema\, with an annual endowment of EUR 1.5 million backin
 g up to 14 feature film projects across development\, production\, and pos
 t-production. The Fund imposes NO restrictions on geography\, theme\, genr
 e\, or language and does not participate as a co-producer\, guaranteeing c
 omplete artistic freedom to filmmakers. It supports both established autho
 rs and new talents\, as well as research projects. WHICH TRACKS ARE STILL 
 OPEN: the 2026 call opened 30 June 2026 and runs on two separate deadlines
 . The projects-in-production track has already CLOSED (6 August 2026). Dev
 elopment and post-production remain open to 10 September 2026\, which is t
 he deadline this card now tracks. Post-production applicants can keep work
 ing after submitting: a rough cut may be supplied up to 20 November 2026. 
 SELECTION is based exclusively on quality\, originality\, vision\, and the
  strength and reliability of the applicant structure\; projects are evalua
 ted by independent readers and external consultants\, with final selection
  and grant amounts determined by a committee appointed by Fondazione Prada
  and composed of prominent figures from cinema and culture. No fixed per-s
 tage grant bands are published\, so the committee sets each award. ELIGIBI
 LITY: applications may be submitted only by a production company involved 
 in the project\, and that company remains solely responsible for meeting a
 ll requirements and conditions\; obligations of selected beneficiaries are
  governed by a contract with Fondazione Prada. Open worldwide\, with no ge
 ographic restriction at all. PHISHING WARNING FROM THE FUNDER: all officia
 l communications about the Film Fund come only from addresses in the fonda
 zioneprada.org domain. Treat anything from another domain as a probable fr
 aud or phishing attempt and verify before responding. The second edition's
  selected projects are announced February 2027. Application documents are 
 on the Fondazione Prada Film Fund page\; questions to filmfund@fondazionep
 rada.org.\n\nOrganisation: Fondazione Prada\nLocation: Milan\, Italy-based
  fund\; open worldwide to independent producers and production companies.\
 nAward: EUR 1.5 million annual endowment supporting up to 14 projects. Ind
 ividual grant amounts are set by the Fondazione Prada selection committee 
 (no fixed per-stage bands published). No application fee.\nDuration: Featu
 re film funding at development\, production or post-production stage. The 
 2026 call opened 30 June 2026. Projects in production closed 6 August 2026
 \; projects in development and post-production close 10 September 2026. Po
 st-production projects may supply a rough cut until 20 November 2026\, wit
 h selections announced February 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.fondazioneprada
 .org/film-fund/?lang=en&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.fondazioneprada.org/film-fund/?lang=en&utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Milan\, Italy-based fund\; open worldwide to independent producers
  and production companies.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:liu-shiming-artist-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Liu Shiming Art Foundation: Artist Grants 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Liu Shiming Art Foundation's annual Artist Grants (fourth e
 dition) award up to five grants of USD 5\,000 each to early-career visual 
 artists to create new work exploring connections between traditional\, cul
 tural\, or historical influences and contemporary artistic practice. ELIGI
 BILITY: visual artists in the first decade of their career (two to ten yea
 rs practicing professionally)\; applicants must have received a studio-art
 s degree between 2016 and 2024\, or had their debut gallery or juried-exhi
 bition show between 2016 and 2026. Open to artists of any country\; the ap
 plication and all supporting materials must be in English. TIMELINE: appli
 cations open 1 June 2026\; close 31 August 2026\; recipients notified by 2
  December 2026. Apply via the Foundation's grants page.\n\nOrganisation: L
 iu Shiming Art Foundation\nLocation: Open to artists of any country\; appl
 ication must be in English.\nAward: Up to five grants of USD 5\,000 each. 
 Disbursed in two payments (USD 3\,000 by 15 January 2027 and USD 2\,000 on
  project completion). No application fee.\nDuration: Project grant for new
  work\n\nMore: https://www.lsmartfund.org/grants?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.lsmartfund.org/grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open to artists of any country\; application must be in English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:club-nothing-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260809
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260810
SUMMARY:Deadline: Club Nothing: Community Music Fund
DESCRIPTION:Club Nothing is a global events series and USD 40\,000 fund fro
 m the tech brand Nothing\, supporting organisers\, artists\, and collectiv
 es creating new music experiences. The fund will award four individuals or
  collectives USD 10\,000 each to throw a club event\, series\, or festival
  later this year\, backing disruptors bringing new sounds and experiences 
 to their communities through nightlife anywhere in the world. Applications
  are judged by a panel including DJ and producer Manuka Honey (Marissa Mal
 ik)\, Nothing Global Senior Community Manager and Madruga Festival co-foun
 der Erica Travis\, Nothing Global Head of Communications Shavone Charles\,
  Dazed Music Editor Solomon Pace-McCarrick\, A&R and music-publishing foun
 der James Supreme\, and music-industry professional Layla Mustafa Rock. Ap
 plications close 9 August 2026\; winners announced late August 2026. Learn
  more and apply at nothing.tech/club-nothing (details also posted at https
 ://nothing.community/d/59214-want-10000-to-throw-a-party). See full terms 
 at nothing.tech/club-nothing/terms-and-conditions.\n\nOrganisation: Nothin
 g\nLocation: Anywhere in the world.\nAward: USD 40\,000 fund total\; four 
 individuals or collectives each receive USD 10\,000 to produce a club even
 t\, series\, or festival. No application fee.\nDuration: Event\, series\, 
 or festival to take place later in 2026\; winners announced late August 20
 26.\n\nMore: https://nothing.tech/club-nothing?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://nothing.tech/club-nothing?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rps-eamonn-mccabe-bursary-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:Deadline: Eamonn McCabe Bursary 2026 (Royal Photographic Society)
DESCRIPTION:The Eamonn McCabe Bursary\, launched in 2024\, commemorates the
  life of photojournalist Eamonn McCabe (1948-2022)\, who made his name as 
 a sports photographer before moving to wider editorial work\, mainly for T
 he Observer and The Guardian\, and who supported a generation of photograp
 hers from the 1980s to the 2020s. Run by the RPS in partnership with McCab
 e's family and The Guardian\, this international bursary continues that le
 gacy. AWARD: GBP 3\,000 to a photographer aged 30 years or under to delive
 r a photography project responding to the theme of 'sporting endeavour'\, 
 which can be interpreted as widely as the applicant wishes\, though the ge
 neral approach should be suitable for publication. The project should norm
 ally be new\, not previously exhibited or published. As well as profession
 al sports\, the call particularly encourages projects covering grassroots 
 and community activities (for example\, addressing issues such as mental h
 ealth or supporting displaced communities)\, and welcomes creative interpr
 etations of the theme. The completed project will be published by The Guar
 dian and the RPS. ELIGIBILITY: applicants must be aged 30 years or under o
 n the closing date. PROCESS: interviews via Zoom in September\; recipient 
 announced by the end of September\; project completed within one year of a
 ward. Apply via the RPS application portal using RPS Account credentials. 
 Closing date 3 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: The Royal Photographic Societ
 y (RPS)\, in partnership with Eamonn McCabe's family and The Guardian\nLoc
 ation: International bursary. Applicants must be aged 30 years or under on
  the closing date. Interviews held via Zoom.\nAward: GBP 3\,000 to deliver
  a photography project on the theme of 'sporting endeavour'. The completed
  project will be published by The Guardian and the RPS\, who will work wit
 h the recipient to bring the project to a wider audience.\nDuration: The p
 roject should be completed within one year of being awarded.\n\nMore: http
 s://rps.org/opportunities/bursaries/eamonn-mccabe-bursary/?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://rps.org/opportunities/bursaries/eamonn-mccabe-bursary/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:International bursary. Applicants must be aged 30 years or under o
 n the closing date. Interviews held via Zoom.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:textile-exchange-atmos-fashion-regenerated-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260720
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260721
SUMMARY:Deadline: Textile Exchange x Atmos: Fashion Regenerated 2026
DESCRIPTION:Fashion Regenerated is an open call from Textile Exchange and A
 tmos. Winners are selected by a panel of expert judges and\, for the first
  time\, a public vote. The shortlist is promoted through Textile Exchange 
 and Atmos\, amplifying inspirational stories to an engaged audience of tho
 usands. The overall winner receives a paid collaborative commission to the
  value of USD 10\,000 with Textile Exchange to develop a new body of work 
 documenting the evidence of regeneration\, working closely with the team t
 o identify the right story and access\; the winning work is published thro
 ugh Atmos\, Textile Exchange\, and shown to an audience of more than 1\,30
 0 changemakers at the 2026 Textile Exchange conference. Two runners-up hav
 e their work promoted by Textile Exchange and displayed at the conference 
 exhibition\, and there is also a USD 2\,000 cash prize. Check the call sit
 e for full eligibility and submission details. Deadline: 20 July 2026.\n\n
 Organisation: Textile Exchange (with Atmos)\nLocation: Open call\; work to
  be promoted globally through Textile Exchange and Atmos and exhibited at 
 the 2026 Textile Exchange conference.\nAward: Overall winner: a paid colla
 borative commission worth USD 10\,000 with Textile Exchange to develop a n
 ew body of work documenting the evidence of regeneration\, published throu
 gh Atmos and Textile Exchange and shown at the 2026 conference. Two runner
 s-up: work promoted by Textile Exchange and displayed at the conference ex
 hibition\, plus a USD 2\,000 cash prize.\nDuration: One-off commission/pri
 ze.\n\nMore: https://site.picter.com/fashion-regenerated-2026?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://site.picter.com/fashion-regenerated-2026?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open call\; work to be promoted globally through Textile Exchange 
 and Atmos and exhibited at the 2026 Textile Exchange conference.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:who-let-the-docs-out-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260710
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260711
SUMMARY:Deadline: Who Let The Docs Out: Documentary Production Grants (2026
  Cycles)
DESCRIPTION:Who Let The Docs Out provides funding across five stages of doc
 umentary production: Research (USD 8\,000)\, Development/Sizzle (USD 15\,0
 00)\, Production (USD 50\,000)\, Post-Production (USD 50\,000)\, and Impac
 t Campaign (USD 30\,000). Funding is organized into thematic funds such as
  the Coexistence Documentary Fund and the Automation & Humanity Documentar
 y Fund. There are three funding cycles per year\, each with its own applic
 ation window and the documentary stages it supports. 2026 SPRING CYCLE (Re
 search & Development Grants): applications open 16 February 2026\, close 1
 6 March 2026\; notification mid-April 2026\; required program commitment M
 ay-July (monthly virtual sessions). 2026 SUMMER CYCLE (Research\, Developm
 ent & Production Grants): applications open 5 June 2026\, close 10 July 20
 26\; notification 15 August 2026\; required program commitment September-N
 ovember (monthly virtual sessions). 2026 AUTUMN CYCLE (Research\, Developm
 ent & Post-Production Grants): applications open 1 October 2026\, close 15
  November 2026\; notification 15 December 2026\; required program commitme
 nt January-March (monthly virtual sessions). Awarded filmmakers must commi
 t to monthly virtual sessions during their cycle. The deadline shown here 
 is the currently open Summer Cycle close date (10 July 2026)\; see the fun
 der's site for full eligibility and thematic-fund details\, or contact hel
 lo@wholethedocsout.org.\n\nOrganisation: Who Let The Docs Out\nLocation: R
 emote program (monthly virtual sessions)\; documentary projects\nAward: St
 age-based funding: Research USD 8\,000\; Development/Sizzle USD 15\,000\; 
 Production USD 50\,000\; Post-Production USD 50\,000\; Impact Campaign USD
  30\,000. No application fee.\nDuration: Required program commitment of ro
 ughly three months of monthly virtual sessions during the awarded cycle\n\
 nMore: https://www.docsout.org/grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.docsout.org/grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote program (monthly virtual sessions)\; documentary projects
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sffilm-documentary-film-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260707
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260708
SUMMARY:Deadline: SFFILM Documentary Film Fund 2026
DESCRIPTION:SFFILM's Documentary Film Fund supports feature-length document
 aries in post-production with compelling stories and an innovative approac
 h to the craft. ELIGIBILITY: applicants 18 or older in a key creative role
  (director or producer)\; feature-length documentary (60+ minutes) within 
 roughly three months of completing post-production\; need not be US-based.
  Regular deadline 9 June 2026 ($30 fee)\; final deadline 7 July 2026 ($50 
 fee). Distinct from the SFFILM Rainin Grant. Apply via the SFFILM grants p
 ortal.\n\nOrganisation: SFFILM\nLocation: Remote / worldwide (need not be 
 US-based)\nAward: $10\,000 to $20\,000 per project (3 to 6 projects per ye
 ar). Application fee: $30 (regular deadline) or $50 (final deadline).\nDur
 ation: Project-based grant\n\nMore: https://sffilm.org/documentary-film-fu
 nd/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sffilm.org/documentary-film-fund/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / worldwide (need not be US-based)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:day-job-short-film-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:Deadline: Day Job: Short Film Fund 2026
DESCRIPTION:Short film competition from Day Job Films created to give auteu
 r directors full creative freedom\, awarding a production budget of up to 
 GBP 7\,000 to make a short film with no producer interference or commercia
 l agenda. Open to animation\, live-action and documentary projects. Runs i
 n three rounds: (1) a pitch deck outlining concept\, story\, key character
 s and visual style\; (2) a full script for those who progress\; and (3) an
  interview to discuss the vision and execution. A panel of industry profes
 sionals judges the pitch deck\, script and interview\, with at least one t
 eam member reading each pitch deck and script in full. The winner receives
  full creative control over the project. ELIGIBILITY: applicants can be fr
 om anywhere worldwide\, but all production must take place in the UK\; app
 licants must have a producer on board who is separate from the director/wr
 iter. Applicants may optionally include a plan for adapting the script int
 o a feature-length film (this does not affect the outcome). Submissions op
 en February 10\, 2026 and close August 10\, 2026. Enquiries: hello@dayjobf
 ilms.com.\n\nOrganisation: Day Job Films\nLocation: Worldwide applicants\;
  all production must take place in the UK\nAward: Production budget of up 
 to GBP 7\,000\, with full creative control and no producer or external int
 erference. No application fee.\nDuration: Per short film project\n\nMore: 
 https://www.dayjobfilms.com/short-film-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.dayjobfilms.com/short-film-fund?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide applicants\; all production must take place in the UK
END:VEVENT
